off in Sanford Stadium.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uga-between-the-hedges","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Between the Hedges","title":"See “Between the Hedges”","subtitle":"Sanford Stadium playing field","notes":"Look down to the Chinese privet hedge border around Sanford’s field and connect the landscape feature to UGA’s familiar home-field phrase.","short_summary":"The hedge-lined field behind UGA’s defining stadium nickname.","evidence_claim":"UGA Athletics documents “Between the Hedges” as a reference to Sanford Stadium dating to the early 1930s and identifies the Chinese privet hedges around the field.","source_url":"https://georgiadogs.com/sports/2017/6/16/traditions/","source_title":"Georgia Bulldogs Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2017-06-16","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Visible around Sanford Stadium’s playing field during stadium access or events.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uga-silver-britches","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Silver Britches","title":"Spot the Silver Britches","subtitle":"Georgia football uniform tradition","notes":"At a Georgia football game, look for the silver pants that give the Bulldogs’ “Silver Britches” tradition its visual signature.","short_summary":"A football-uniform nickname with a long UGA history.","evidence_claim":"UGA Athletics says “Silver Britches” began under Coach Wally Butts and was reintroduced by Coach Vince Dooley in 1980.","source_url":"https://georgiadogs.com/sports/2017/6/16/traditions/","source_title":"Georgia Bulldogs Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2017-06-16","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Associated with Georgia football uniforms at games and team appearances.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"sub